## Glossary

- NC-CPA / NC-ROAS: New-customer CPA / ROAS. CAC measured on new customers only, used to compare paid channels on incremental acquisition. Always written with the hyphen. Never "NCPA".
- MTA (Multi-touch attribution): Distributes credit for a conversion across every ad touchpoint in the customer journey, instead of giving 100% credit to last click.
- MCP (Model Context Protocol): Anthropic's open protocol for LLMs to query external tools. The Converge MCP lets Claude, ChatGPT, n8n, Zapier, or any MCP-compatible client hit the same data that powers the dashboards.
- Server-side tracking: Conversion events sent from your server to ad platforms (via Conversions API and equivalents) instead of the browser. 
- CAPI: Meta's Conversions API. The standard destination for server-side conversion events on Meta.

